@startuml
' Participants
box "Seller" #pink 
participant "Seller" as Seller
end box
box "Buyer" #lightyellow 
participant "Buyer (Payer)" as Buyer
end box
box "Investor" #lightgreen
participant "Investor" as Investor
participant "Investor Cash\nAccount" as Cash
end box

box "PrimeRevenue Platform" #lightblue
participant "PrimeRevenue\nPlatform" as PR
participant "Market / Listing" as Market
participant "Investor Auto\nSubscription Engine" as Auto
end box

== Seller delivers goods to Buyer ==
Seller -> Buyer: Deliver goods / services
activate Buyer
Buyer -> Seller: Acknowledge receipt
deactivate Buyer

== Seller creates Time Draft ==
Seller -> PR: Submit invoice ($100 due in 30d)
activate PR
PR -> PR: Create Time Draft (rulebook)
PR -> Market: Publish Time Draft
deactivate PR

note over Investor,Auto
Investor may purchase manually or use an automated
"rolling investment" (subscription) to auto-buy matching drafts
end note

== Manual purchase (one-off) ==
Investor -> PR: Purchase Time Draft ($95)
PR -> Seller: Initiate T+1 settlement (send $95 next day)
PR -> Investor: Confirm purchase

== Automated (rolling) purchase ==
loop continuous / periodic
  Auto -> PR: Poll for Time Drafts (criteria: rating, yield, tenure)
  PR -> Auto: Return matching Time Draft
  Auto -> Cash: Check available balance
  alt sufficient funds
    Cash --> Auto: Reserve $95 (purchase price)
    Auto -> PR: Execute Purchase ($95)
    PR -> Investor: Confirm purchase
    PR -> Seller: Initiate T+1 settlement (send $95 next day)
  else insufficient funds
    Auto -> Investor: Notify failed purchase (or queue)
    note right: Lack of visibility into pre-funded cash accounts\nmay cause failed transactions or negative balances
  end
end



== Maturity / Settlement ==
Buyer -> PR: Pay invoice ($100) on due date
activate PR
PR -> Investor: Transfer face value $100 (settlement to investor)
deactivate PR

note over Investor
Investor realizes return (e.g., ~5.2% if buyer pays on time)
end note

@enduml
